{title: 216 - When the Roll Is Called Up Yonder}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #216 • ROLL CALL • 15.11.15.11.8.8}
{lyricist: J. M. Black}
{composer: J. M. Black}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 216}
{meta: tune ROLL CALL}
{meta: meter 15.11.15.11.8.8}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]When the trumpet of the Lord shall sound, and [Em]time shall be no [G]more,
[G]And the morning breaks, eternal, [Am]bright and [F#dim]fair;
[G]When the saved of earth shall gather [Em]over [G]on the other [F#dim]shore,
[F#dim]And the roll is called up yonder, [G]I'll be there.
[G]When the roll [D]is called up yonder,
[G]When the roll is [C]called up [D7]yonder,
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D7]When the roll is called up yonder,
[Em]When the roll is [D]called up yonder,
[C]When the roll is called up yonder,
[C/G]When the [G]roll is called up yonder, I'll be there.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]On that bright and cloudless [Em]morning,
[G]when the dead in Christ shall [Am]rise,
[G]And the glory of [Em]His resurection [G]share;
[F#dim]When His chosen ones [G]shall gather
[G]to their home [D]beyond the skies,
[G]And the roll is called up [C]yonder, I'll [D7]be there.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Let us labor for the [Em]Master
[G]from the dawn till setting [Am]sun,
[G]Let us talk of all [Em]His wondrous [G]love and care,
[F#dim]Then, when all of life is [G]over,
[G]and our work [D]on earth is done,
[G]And the roll is called up [C]yonder I'll [D7]be there.
{end_of_verse}
